      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The main aim of the treatment of hypertension is to reduce the incidence and severity of its complications. Despite some bias affecting the major clinical trials of diuretics and/or beta blockers, the results of the meta-analysis taking them into account demonstrate the effectiveness of the prevention of cerebrovascular complications and the less effective prevention of coronary complications. Progress can be hoped for as a result of new therapeutic categories (converting enzyme inhibitors, calcium channel inhibitors ...) and to a greater extent from new treatment strategies, involving better identification of \"genuinely high risk\" subjects."},
